Chapter: SceneOpenCostTest
  cites Works chapter GopScene
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 What a 3D pane's `-open` allocates, which is D.5's `want`.

 A pane that reuses a buried hole has to ask for a size before it enters,
 and no pane had that size measured. This chapter measures the 3D pane's,
 because `gsc-new` is the bounded case: two buffers and a record, nothing
 that grows afterwards. Files and the Browser are the panes whose STEP
 stores durable state, so under D.5's first sizing rule they are the worst
 first candidates rather than the obvious ones.

 THE FIRST LINE IS THE CONTROL. `alloc-bytes 0` advances the bump allocator
 by nothing and answers the frontier, so a difference across a call is what
 that call made permanent. Two reads with nothing between them must differ
 by zero; any other answer means the instrument allocates and every number
 below is its own footprint (L-FALSIF).

 THE SECOND SIZE IS WHAT MAKES THE NUMBER MEAN ANYTHING. One reading cannot
 tell a size that follows the content box from a constant, and a hole sized
 from a constant would be right at one geometry and wrong at every other.
 The two boxes differ by 100 rows of 320, and `gsc-new` allocates a colour
 buffer and a depth buffer of four bytes a pixel each, so the difference
 must be exactly 320 * 100 * 8. That is a prediction the machine confirms,
 not a bound recorded from whatever it happened to say (L-COUNT).

 `cursor-hide` reads `peek-32 cs 0` and answers immediately when the cell is
 zero, so a zeroed cell keeps this chapter off the glass; `gpu` 0 skips the
 texture upload. Neither is a shortcut around the measurement: both are the
 branches `gsc-new` takes on a desk with no cursor shown and no GPU.

Section: Body

  soc-yn : Boolean -> Text
  soc-yn (v) = if v then "PASS" else "FAIL"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Gpu.Compute, Gpu.Memory] Nothing = act
    let c0 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let c1 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let cs = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in act
      print-line-uni ("CONTROL, the probe allocates nothing: " & soc-yn (c1 - c0 == 0))
      let a0 = alloc-bytes 0
      in act
        sp1 <- gsc-new 4096 1600 cs 0 0 320 200
        let a1 = alloc-bytes 0
        in act
          sp2 <- gsc-new 4096 1600 cs 0 0 320 300
          let a2 = alloc-bytes 0
          in let burn = alloc-bytes 64
          in let a3 = alloc-bytes 0
          in act
            print-line-uni ("want at 320x200: " & integer-to-text (a1 - a0))
            print-line-uni ("want at 320x300: " & integer-to-text (a2 - a1))
            print-line-uni ("want follows the box at 8 bytes a pixel: " & soc-yn (a2 - a1 - (a1 - a0) == 320 * 100 * 8))
            print-line-uni ("the buffers are the whole of it: " & soc-yn (a1 - a0 > 320 * 200 * 8))
            print-line-uni ("CONTROL, the probe can see 64: " & soc-yn (a3 - a2 >= 64))
            print-line-uni ("the pane keeps its own size: " & soc-yn (sp1.sp-bw == 320 & sp1.sp-bh == 200 & sp2.sp-bh == 300))
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
